## Report
Rubric-driven validation: Built debug tests (`cargo test -p server-core --lib --no-run`) and ran the existing unit test for unauthorized ListParts (`cargo test -p server-core --lib authorize_list_parts_rejects_non_owner_requester -- --nocapture`), which passed and confirms AccessDenied for non-owner requests (log in artifacts). Attempts to use valgrind/gdb failed because the tools are not installed. Code inspection shows the pre-auth metadata read: in `authorize_list_parts`, the call to `storage_node.list_multipart_parts_for_upload(...)` happens before the `requester_can_manage_multipart_upload(...)` authorization check (crates/server-core/src/coordinator/authz.rs:4258-4289). The storage helper immediately loads the upload metadata and invokes `pg.list_multipart_parts(...)` (crates/storage/src/node.rs:1025-1038), which in turn executes SQL queries and materializes multipart part records into memory (crates/storage/src/pg_store.rs:5335-5398). This confirms that an unauthorized ListParts request still triggers SQLite reads and row materialization before AccessDenied, creating a resource-consumption/timing side effect as described.

